{"seconds": 42.1, "exit": 0, "final": "After Bd4+, White is still up a queen (just took it with Bxg2). White plays Ke1 or another king move, and is decisively winning. This is clearly the best move.\n\n**Best move: Nf4**\n\n**Main line:** Nf4 Qxg2+ Bxg2 Bd4+ Ke1 (or Ke2/Kf3)\n\n**Motif:** Fork (the knight attacks both the bishop and queen, forcing the queen into a vulnerable square where it's trapped and captured)\n\n**Coaching note:** When your opponent's queen becomes aggressive on h2, look for quiet moves that attack multiple pieces. Nf4 forks the bishop and queen, and when Black captures on g2 with check, the queen is trapped by three White pieces! Always count defenders when the enemy queen dares to attack your king\u2014it often means it's overextended and can be caught.\n\n```json\n{\"move\": \"Nf4\", \"line\": [\"Nf4\", \"Qxg2+\", \"Bxg2\", \"Bd4+\", \"Ke1\", \"Bxf1\"], \"motifs\": [\"fork\", \"quietMove\"]}\n```", "tool_calls": [{"tool": "skill", "args": {"skill": "chess-coach"}}, {"tool": "chess-eyes-board", "args": {"fen": "r3k1nr/p2b1ppp/2p5/3pb3/4P3/P4B2/1PPBNKPq/R2Q1R2 w kq - 1 20"}}, {"tool": "chess-eyes-threats", "args": {"fen": "r3k1nr/p2b1ppp/2p5/3pb3/4P3/P4B2/1PPBNKPq/R2Q1R2 w kq - 1 20"}}, {"tool": "chess-eyes-legal_moves", "args": {"fen": "r3k1nr/p2b1ppp/2p5/3pb3/4P3/P4B2/1PPBNKPq/R2Q1R2 w kq - 1 20"}}, {"tool": "chess-eyes-inspect_move", "args": {"fen": "r3k1nr/p2b1ppp/2p5/3pb3/4P3/P4B2/1PPBNKPq/R2Q1R2 w kq - 1 20", "move": "Nf4"}}, {"tool": "chess-eyes-inspect_move", "args": {"fen": "r3k1nr/p2b1ppp/2p5/3pb3/4P3/P4B2/1PPBNKPq/R2Q1R2 w kq - 1 20", "move": "Rh1"}}, {"tool": "chess-eyes-inspect_move", "args": {"fen": "r3k1nr/p2b1ppp/2p5/3pb3/4P3/P4B2/1PPBNKPq/R2Q1R2 w kq - 1 20", "move": "Ng3"}}, {"tool": "chess-eyes-inspect_move", "args": {"fen": "r3k1nr/p2b1ppp/2p5/3pb3/4P3/P4B2/1PPBNKPq/R2Q1R2 w kq - 1 20", "move": "exd5"}}, {"tool": "chess-eyes-inspect_move", "args": {"fen": "r3k1nr/p2b1ppp/2p5/3Pb3/8/P4B2/1PPBNKPq/R2Q1R2 b kq - 0 20", "move":